    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d260">

                <pb facs="0418" n="332" sameAs="frus:frus1927v01/pg332"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">721.2315/325: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Peru</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Poindexter</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-01-06T10:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 6,
                                1927—10 a.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>1. Embassy’s telegram number 110, December 30, 6 p.m. It being important to have
                    as many causes of dissension between the Latin American Republics as possible
                    removed before the Pan American Conference convenes,<anchor n="72"
                        xml:id="d260-f1"/> you should take up this question again with the Foreign
                    Minister or with the President, or both. The Department <pb facs="0419" n="333"
                        xml:id="pg333"/> has been informed that there is real danger that Colombia
                    may sever diplomatic relations if the treaty is not ratified after repeated
                    promises of President Leguía. Such action would naturally cause serious
                    embarrassment to the Government of the United States which sponsored the
                        protocol.<anchor n="73" xml:id="d260-f2"/></p>
                <p>The Department does not think there is any use in discussing the question with
                    Velarde. …</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d260-f1" n="72" xml:id="d260-f1-content">
                <p>Convened at Habana, Jan. 16 to Feb. 20, 1928.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d260-f2" n="73" xml:id="d260-f2-content">
                <p>See procès-verbal of a meeting between representatives of the United States,
                    Peru, Colombia, and Brazil, Mar. 4, 1925, at Washington, <ref
                        target="frus1925v01#pg_461"><hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>,
                        1925, vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps">i</hi>, p. 461</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
